course: dictionary
lesson: 3100
title: Eight, and the clues around it
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Eight is a number word that means 8, one more than seven. Like any word, it has clues around it. «Most spiders have eight eyes» is a sentence about spiders, and the word eight tells you how many.
explain: Eight is used to count many things: legs, arms, sides and even the time on a clock. «A spider is not an insect: it has eight legs, two body parts and no antennae or wings.» Here eight counts legs. Check by swapping in the number 8: "it has 8 legs" still makes sense.
explain: Context can also show you how numbers join together. «A squid or cuttlefish has eight arms plus two longer tentacles» gives ten limbs in all. Eight plus two makes ten, so the words around eight help you add them up.
fact: Eight is the number 8, one more than seven.
fact: Eight is the count of legs on a spider and of arms on an octopus.
fact: «The deepest fish ever filmed was a snailfish at over eight kilometres.» Here eight is part of a measurement.
fact: The multiples of eight are 8, 16, 24 and 32.
fact: A spider is not an insect: it has eight legs and two body parts, while an insect has six legs and three body parts.
exercise: «A spider is not an insect: it has eight legs, two body parts and no antennae or wings.» How many legs does a spider have? | Two | Six | Ten | *Eight
exercise: «A squid or cuttlefish has eight arms plus two longer tentacles.» How many arms does a squid have? | Two | *Eight | Ten | Four
exercise: Eight is one more than which number? | Nine | Six | Ten | *Seven
test: Multiples of eight are 8, 16, 24 and 32. Which of these numbers is a multiple of eight? | *Sixteen | Twenty | Twelve | Thirty
test: Which of these numbers is one more than seven? | Nine | Ten | Six | *Eight
exam: «Most spiders have eight eyes, but many see poorly and rely on touch and vibration.» Which word tells you how many eyes most spiders have? | vibration | spiders | *eight | touch
